comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T21:34:35.625Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-07-31: declared provenance dimensions now serialize explicit unavailable values instead of disappearing, and MCP initialization accepts a bounded host provenance map that is resolved into each tool invocation scope. Integration and SDK tests cover schema completeness, bounds, and history semantics; 6,623 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100. The ADR and runtime guide document the cross-surface contract. This item remains active because a paired live harness test must still prove field-for-field CLI/MCP identity parity and disposition the historical mixed records before closure."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:28:49.112Z","harness:claude-code","Reading /proc/<pid>/environ for a long-lived MCP server and comparing it to the tool subprocess's environment turns an inference about missing signals into a fact. Harnesses do not export the same environment to every child they spawn, so any capability that resolves configuration from process.env behaves differently per surface, and a server that snapshots env at startup freezes anything the user can change mid-session."
